{"id":20,"role":"Tool","content":"C:\\github\\YangMills\\src\\lean\\YangMills\\Proofs\\ReflectionPositivity.lean\n-- 1526 lines, 94678 bytes --\n325 |       simp [h_trace_star]\n326 |     _ = ((Matrix.trace (((A⁻¹ : SU N) : Matrix (Fin N) (Fin N) ℂ))).re : ℝ) := by simp [hstar]\n327 | \n328 | /-- The sum over all oriented plaquettes (n; μ, ν) where all four corners have\n329 | positive signed time. This is the correct positive-time part of the\n330 | Osterwalder-Seiler decomposition. -/\n331 | noncomputable def wilsonActionOSPositive (N T L : ℕ) (β : ℝ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L]\n332 |     (U : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L)) : ℝ :=\n333 |   ∑ n : PeriodicSite T L, ∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ ν : Fin 4,\n334 |     if signedTime T n.time > 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time > 0 ∧\n335 |        signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time > 0 ∧\n336 |        signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time > 0 then\n337 |       plaquetteContribution N β U n μ ν\n338 |     else 0\n339 | \n340 | /-- The sum over all oriented plaquettes (n; μ, ν) where all four corners have\n341 | negative signed time. This is the correct negative-time part of the\n342 | Osterwalder-Seiler decomposition. -/\n343 | noncomputable def wilsonActionOSNegative (N T L : ℕ) (β : ℝ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L]\n344 |     (U : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L)) : ℝ :=\n345 |   ∑ n : PeriodicSite T L, ∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ ν : Fin 4,\n346 |     if signedTime T n.time < 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time < 0 ∧\n347 |        signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time < 0 ∧\n348 |        signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time < 0 then\n349 |       plaquetteContribution N β U n μ ν\n350 |     else 0\n351 | \n352 | /-- The sum over the remaining oriented plaquettes (those with corners on both sides\n353 | of the time interface). This is the interface part of the\n354 | Osterwalder-Seiler decomposition. -/\n355 | noncomputable def wilsonActionOSInterface (N T L : ℕ) (β : ℝ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L]\n356 |     (U : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L)) : ℝ :=\n357 |   ∑ n : PeriodicSite T L, ∑ μ : Fin 4, ∑ ν : Fin 4,\n358 |     if ¬ (signedTime T n.time > 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time > 0 ∧\n359 |           signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time > 0 ∧\n360 |           signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time > 0) ∧\n361 |        ¬ (signedTime T n.time < 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time < 0 ∧\n362 |           signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time < 0 ∧\n363 |           signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time < 0) then\n364 |       plaquetteContribution N β U n μ ν\n365 |     else 0\n366 | \n367 | /--\n368 | For each oriented plaquette (n; μ, ν), exactly one of the three conditions holds:\n369 | positive (all corners > 0), negative (all corners < 0), or interface (the rest).\n370 | -/\n371 | lemma plaquette_classification (T L : ℕ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L] (n : PeriodicSite T L) (μ ν : Fin 4) :\n372 |     (signedTime T n.time > 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time > 0 ∧\n373 |      signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time > 0 ∧\n374 |      signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time > 0) ∨\n375 |     (signedTime T n.time < 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time < 0 ∧\n376 |      signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time < 0 ∧\n377 |      signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time < 0) ∨\n378 |     (¬ (signedTime T n.time > 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time > 0 ∧\n379 |         signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time > 0 ∧\n380 |         signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time > 0) ∧\n381 |      ¬ (signedTime T n.time < 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time < 0 ∧\n382 |         signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time < 0 ∧\n383 |         signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time < 0)) := by\n384 |   by_cases hpos : signedTime T n.time > 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time > 0 ∧\n385 |                   signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time > 0 ∧\n386 |                   signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time > 0\n387 |   · exact Or.inl hpos\n388 |   · by_cases hneg : signedTime T n.time < 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time < 0 ∧\n389 |                    signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time < 0 ∧\n390 |                    signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time < 0\n391 |     · exact Or.inr (Or.inl hneg)\n392 |     · exact Or.inr (Or.inr ⟨hpos, hneg⟩)\n393 | \n394 | /--\n395 | The total Wilson action decomposes into positive, negative, and interface parts\n396 | (plaquette-based OS decomposition):\n397 |     S_W = S_OS⁺ + S_OS⁻ + S_OS_int\n398 | -/\n399 | lemma total_decomposition_os_periodic (N T L : ℕ) (β : ℝ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L]\n400 |     (U : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L)) :\n401 |     wilsonActionFinite N β (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)) U =\n402 |     wilsonActionOSPositive N T L β U +\n403 |     wilsonActionOSNegative N T L β U +\n404 |     wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β U := by\n405 |   unfold wilsonActionOSPositive wilsonActionOSNegative wilsonActionOSInterface wilsonActionFinite\n406 |   have h_split (n : PeriodicSite T L) (μ ν : Fin 4) : plaquetteContribution N β U n μ ν =\n407 |     (if signedTime T n.time > 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time > 0 ∧\n408 |          signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time > 0 ∧\n409 |          signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time > 0 then\n410 |       plaquetteContribution N β U n μ ν else 0) +\n411 |     (if signedTime T n.time < 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time < 0 ∧\n412 |          signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time < 0 ∧\n413 |          signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time < 0 then\n414 |       plaquetteContribution N β U n μ ν else 0) +\n415 |     (if ¬ (signedTime T n.time > 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time > 0 ∧\n416 |           signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time > 0 ∧\n417 |           signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time > 0) ∧\n418 |        ¬ (signedTime T n.time < 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time < 0 ∧\n419 |           signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time < 0 ∧\n420 |           signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time < 0) then\n421 |       plaquetteContribution N β U n μ ν else 0) := by\n422 |     rcases plaquette_classification T L n μ ν with (⟨h1, h2, h3, h4⟩|⟨h1, h2, h3, h4⟩|⟨hnpos, hnneg⟩)\n423 |     · -- All signed times > 0\n424 |       have h_neg : ¬ (signedTime T n.time < 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time < 0 ∧\n425 |           signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time < 0 ∧\n426 |           signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time < 0) := by\n427 |         intro h; rcases h with ⟨hn1, hn2, hn3, hn4⟩; have := h1; linarith\n428 |       have h_int : ¬ (¬ (signedTime T n.time > 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time > 0 ∧\n429 |           signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time > 0 ∧\n430 |           signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time > 0) ∧\n431 |         ¬ (signedTime T n.time < 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time < 0 ∧\n432 |           signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time < 0 ∧\n433 |           signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time < 0)) := by\n434 |         intro h; rcases h with ⟨hnpos', hnneg'⟩; apply hnpos'; exact ⟨h1, h2, h3, h4⟩\n435 |       calc\n436 |         plaquetteContribution N β U n μ ν\n437 |             = (plaquetteContribution N β U n μ ν) + 0 + 0 := by ring\n438 |         _ = (if signedTime T n.time > 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time > 0 ∧\n439 |               signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time > 0 ∧\n440 |               signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time > 0 then\n441 |               plaquetteContribution N β U n μ ν else 0) +\n442 |             (if signedTime T n.time < 0 ∧ signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ).time < 0 ∧\n443 |               signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L (addVectorPeriodic T L n μ) ν).time < 0 ∧\n444 |               signedTime T (addVectorPeriodic T L n ν).time < 0 then\n\n... 1082 more line(s) below (use offset=445 to continue reading)","timestamp":1784083666,"token_count":2679,"tool_call_id":"call_00_HuIdr9iwUEqeLhY6B2dh5473","full_token_estimate":1952,"tool_meta":{"tool_name":"read_file","file_path":"src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/ReflectionPositivity.lean","old_text":null,"new_text":null,"exit_code":null,"line_count":1526,"byte_count":94678,"is_error":false,"duration_ms":0,"edit_line":null},"turn":5,"is_prune_marker":false}
{"id":21,"role":"Assistant","content":"","timestamp":1784083692,"token_count":0,"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"pattern\": \"def reflectLinkVariable\"}","name":"grep"},"id":"call_00_wJxy4wwYGmTwoUlp8d1J8465","type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"pattern\": \"def reflectObservable\"}","name":"grep"},"id":"call_01_OFIo5TUCaGCb3PkjFiK64150","type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"pattern\": \"def reflectSite\"}","name":"grep"},"id":"call_02_IaXYDVvCro1XNFjQmZC39572","type":"function"}],"full_token_estimate":2243,"reasoning_content":"Now I have a good picture. Let me think about what the transferMatrix_identity needs to prove.\n\nThe LHS of `transferMatrix_identity` is:\n```\n∫ G(U) · G(θU) dμ₀(U)\n```\nwhere `U` ranges over full configurations.\n\nThe RHS is:\n```\n∫ G⁺(u) · (T G⁺)(u) dμ⁺⁰(u)\n```\nwhere `u` ranges over positive+interface configurations.\n\nKey observation: `G(U)` depends only on positive and interface link variables, not on negative link variables. Let me verify this.\n\n`G(U) = f(U) · exp(-β·S_OS⁺(U)) · exp(-β·S_OS_int(U)/2)`\n\n- `wilsonActionOSPositive(N T L β U)` sums over plaquettes where ALL four corners have positive signed time. Since the time coordinate is monotone along links (due to the geometry), the links involved in these plaquettes are at positive-time sites (or possibly interface sites at the boundary of the positive region).\n\nWait, actually a plaquette with all four corners at positive time uses links that connect these corners. The links themselves may connect a positive-time corner to another positive-time corner, so those links are at positive-time sites.\n\nSimilarly, `S_OS_int` involves plaquettes that straddle the time interface - they involve some corners at positive time and some at negative time. The links in these plaquettes connect positive-time sites to interface sites or negative-time sites, etc.\n\nBut the point is: `G(U) = f(U) · exp(-β·S_OS⁺(U)) · exp(-β·S_OS_int(U)/2)` depends only on the positive and interface link variables because:\n- `S_OS⁺(U)` depends only on positive-time links (since all corners are positive, all edges are positive links)\n- `S_OS_int(U)` depends on links that touch the interface, which are interface links (connecting positive/negative/interface sites)\n\nWait, but `f(U)` might depend on ALL links. That's the catch. The function `f` is a general function on all link variables.\n\nActually, let me re-read the statement more carefully:\n\n```lean4\nlemma transferMatrix_identity (f : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L) → ℝ) :\n```\n\nSo `f` is an arbitrary function on all link variables. Then `G(U) = f(U) · exp(-β·S_OS⁺(U)) · exp(-β·S_OS_int(U)/2)` which depends on the full `U` because `f` does.\n\nBut `G_plus(cfg)` is:\n```lean4\nG N T L hT β f (extendLinkVariable N (PeriodicSite T L) (positiveSites T L ∪ interfaceSites T L) cfg)\n```\n\nThis extends `cfg` (a config on positive+interface sites) to a full link variable by setting negative-site links to 1, then applies `G`. So `G_plus` fills missing links with 1.\n\nAnd `G(U)` uses the actual `U` which has real values on negative links.\n\nSo there's a difference: `G(U)` and `G(θU)` use the actual negative links of `U` and `θU`, while `G_plus` fills them with 1.\n\nFor the identity to hold, we need that `f` only depends on positive and interface links, OR that the measure factorization lets us integrate out the negative links and the dependence on them factors out.\n\nWait, actually I think there's a more subtle issue. Let me re-read the handoff:\n\n> **Caveat**: The identity as stated might have a subtle issue — `G_plus` uses `extendLinkVariable` which fills negative-site links with 1, while `G` in the LHS uses the actual negative links from the full config. The identity may only hold if f doesn't depend on negative links, or the measure factorization handles this correctly.\n\nThis is a crucial observation. Let me think about this more carefully.\n\nActually, looking at the definition of `G`:\n```lean4\nnoncomputable def G (N T L : ℕ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L] (hT : Odd T) (β : ℝ)\n    (f : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L) → ℝ) (U : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L)) : ℝ :=\n  f U * Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionOSPositive N T L β U) *\n  Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionOSInterface N T L β U / 2)\n```\n\nAnd `G_plus`:\n```lean4\nnoncomputable def G_plus (N T L : ℕ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L] (hT : Odd T) (β : ℝ)\n    (f : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L) → ℝ) (cfg : PosInterfaceConfig N T L) : ℝ :=\n  G N T L hT β f (extendLinkVariable N (PeriodicSite T L) (positiveSites T L ∪ interfaceSites T L) cfg)\n```\n\nSo `G_plus(cfg) = G(f, extendLinkVariable(positiveSites ∪ interfaceSites, cfg))`.\n\nNow, `extendLinkVariable(sites, cfg)` fills links at sites NOT in `sites` with 1. So for negative-time sites, it fills with 1.\n\nSo `G_plus(U_plus_zero) = f(U_ext) · exp(-β·S_OS⁺(U_ext)) · exp(-β·S_OS_int(U_ext)/2)` where `U_ext` has negative links set to 1.\n\nBut `G(U)` uses the actual `U` which has potentially non-trivial values on negative links.\n\nNow, `S_OS⁺(U)` only depends on positive-time links. And `S_OS_int(U)` depends on interface links. So these two factors are the same for `G(U)` and `G_plus(u)` (when extended properly), because the positive and interface links are the same.\n\nBut `f(U)` in `G(U)` vs `f(extendLinkVariable(..., cfg))` in `G_plus(cfg)` — these differ if `f` depends on negative links!\n\nSo the identity `∫ G(U)·G(θU) dμ₀(U) = ∫ G_plus(u)·(T G_plus)(u) dμ⁺⁰(u)` might NOT hold for general `f`. It only holds if `f` doesn't depend on negative links.\n\nWait, but the reflection positivity lemma `gibbsExpectationPeriodic_reflection_positive` takes `f` as a general function on all link variables. So we need the identity for general `f`.\n\nHmm, let me think about this differently. \n\nActually, let me re-read `integral_G_thetaG_nonneg`:\n\n```lean4\nlemma integral_G_thetaG_nonneg (f : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L) → ℝ) :\n    0 ≤ (∫ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfig N (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L))),\n      G N T L hT β f (extendLinkVariable N (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)) cfg) *\n      G N T L hT β f (reflectLinkVariable N (extendLinkVariable N (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)) cfg))\n      ∂ productHaarMeasure N (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L))) := by\n  rw [transferMatrix_identity N T L hT β f]\n  apply transferMatrix_positive N T L β (G_plus N T L hT β f)\n```\n\nSo the strategy is:\n1. Use `transferMatrix_identity` to rewrite the integral as the RHS\n2. Then apply `transferMatrix_positive` to show the RHS is ≥ 0\n\nNow, `transferMatrix_positive` is proved. So the key is `transferMatrix_identity`.\n\nBut wait, the `gibbsExpectationPeriodic_reflection_positive` in ReflectionPositivity.lean also has this `sorry`:\n\n```lean4\n_ ≥ 0 := by\n  -- GOAL: Prove that ∫ G(U)·G(θU) dμ₀(U) ≥ 0.\n  ...\n  sorry\n```\n\nAnd the comment says: \"Once `transferMatrix_identity` is proved, replace this `sorry` with: apply integral_G_thetaG_nonneg N T L hT β f\"\n\nSo the plan is:\n1. Prove `transferMatrix_identity` \n2. Then `integral_G_thetaG_nonneg` is proved automatically\n3. Then replace the `sorry` in `gibbsExpectationPeriodic_reflection_positive` with `apply integral_G_thetaG_nonneg N T L hT β f`\n\nBut wait, there's a circular import issue: `TransferMatrix.lean` imports `ReflectionPositivity.lean`, so we cannot use `integral_G_thetaG_nonneg` from `TransferMatrix.lean` directly in `ReflectionPositivity.lean`.\n\nThe handoff mentions this: \"Fix: Either (a) move `integral_G_thetaG_nonneg` into `ReflectionPositivity.lean` as a direct proof, or (b) create a third file that imports both and proves the final theorem, or (c) prove `transferMatrix_identity` then restructure imports.\"\n\nLet me focus on proving `transferMatrix_identity` first.\n\nLet me think about the math more carefully. The identity is:\n\n∫_{full} G(U)·G(θU) dμ₀(U) = ∫_{pos+int} G_plus(u)·(T G_plus)(u) dμ⁺⁰(u)\n\nwhere (Tψ)(u) = ∫_{neg} ψ(restrict(merge(u⁻, u))) · exp(-β·S_OS_int(extendToFull(u⁻, u))) dμ⁻(u⁻)\n\nLet me expand both sides.\n\nLHS = ∫_{full} f(U)·f(θU)·exp(-β·S_OS⁺(U))·exp(-β·S_OS_int(U)/2)·exp(-β·S_OS⁺(θU))·exp(-β·S_OS_int(θU)/2) dμ₀(U)\n\nNow, the key properties:\n- S_OS⁺(θU) = S_OS⁻(U) (the reflection swaps positive and negative regions)\n- S_OS_int(θU) = S_OS_int(U) (the interface is invariant under reflection)\n\nThese are already proved as lemmas in ReflectionPositivity.lean.\n\nSo:\nLHS = ∫ f(U)·f(θU)·exp(-β·S_OS⁺(U))·exp(-β·S_OS⁻(U))·exp(-β·S_OS_int(U)) dμ₀(U)\n\nBecause exp(-β·S_OS_int(U)/2)·exp(-β·S_OS_int(U)/2) = exp(-β·S_OS_int(U)).\n\nNow, the measure factorization says μ₀ = μ⁺ × μ⁻ × μ⁰ (up to a measure-preserving isomorphism). So we can write:\n\nLHS = ∫_{μ⁺}∫_{μ⁻}∫_{μ⁰} f(merge(U⁺, U⁻, U⁰))·f(θ(merge(U⁺, U⁻, U⁰)))·exp(-β·S_OS⁺(U⁺))·exp(-β·S_OS⁻(U⁻))·exp(-β·S_OS_int(U⁰)) dμ⁰(U⁰) dμ⁻(U⁻) dμ⁺(U⁺)\n\nActually wait, this is more subtle. The actions depend on the link variables, not just the sites. Let me think about what `S_OS⁺(U)` depends on.\n\n`S_OS⁺(U)` sums over plaquettes where all four corners have positive signed time. The links involved in these plaquettes are links between positive-time sites. These links are exactly the links in `positiveLinks`. So `S_OS⁺(U)` depends only on the SU(N) values on `positiveLinks`.\n\nSimilarly, `S_OS⁻(U)` depends only on `negativeLinks`.\nAnd `S_OS_int(U)` depends only on `interfaceLinks`.\n\nSo:\n- `S_OS⁺(U)` is a function of the restriction of U to positiveLinks\n- `S_OS⁻(U)` is a function of the restriction of U to negativeLinks  \n- `S_OS_int(U)` is a function of the restriction of U to interfaceLinks\n\nBut `f(U)` may depend on ALL links.\n\nNow, `θU` is the reflected configuration. The reflection maps:\n- positiveLinks ↔ negativeLinks (with orientation reversed)\n- interfaceLinks → interfaceLinks (with orientation possibly reversed)\n\nLet me look at `reflectLinkVariable` to understand this.\n\nActually, let me look at how reflection works in the code.","turn":6,"is_prune_marker":false}
