{"id":26,"role":"Tool","content":"C:\\github\\YangMills\\src\\lean\\YangMills\\Lattice.lean\n-- 351 lines, 12085 bytes --\n130 |   | 0 => { n with time := n.time + 1 }\n131 |   | 1 => { n with x := n.x + 1 }\n132 |   | 2 => { n with y := n.y + 1 }\n133 |   | 3 => { n with z := n.z + 1 }\n134 | \n135 | instance (T L : ℕ) : AddVector (PeriodicSite T L) where\n136 |   addVector := addVectorPeriodic T L\n137 | \n138 | /--\n139 | Time reflection on a periodic lattice: maps time t ↦ -t (mod T).\n140 | This is involutive because -(-t) = t in ZMod T.\n141 | -/\n142 | def reflectSitePeriodic (T L : ℕ) (n : PeriodicSite T L) : PeriodicSite T L :=\n143 |   { n with time := -n.time }\n144 | \n145 | instance (T L : ℕ) : ReflectSite (PeriodicSite T L) where\n146 |   reflectSite := reflectSitePeriodic T L\n147 |   involution n := by\n148 |     dsimp [reflectSitePeriodic]; simp\n149 | \n150 | /--\n151 | `reflectSitePeriodic` is involutive: θ(θ n) = n.\n152 | -/\n153 | lemma reflectSitePeriodic_involution (T L : ℕ) (n : PeriodicSite T L) :\n154 |     reflectSitePeriodic T L (reflectSitePeriodic T L n) = n :=\n155 |   ReflectSite.involution n\n156 | \n157 | \n158 | /-- A finite lattice Λ ⊂ ℤ⁴ as a hypercube with spacing a > 0. -/\n159 | structure Lattice (Λ : Type) : Type 1 where\n160 |   /-- Lattice spacing (a real number > 0). -/\n161 |   spacing : ℝ\n162 |   /-- The set of lattice sites. -/\n163 |   sites : Λ\n164 |   /-- Adjacency relation for links. -/\n165 |   links : Λ → Λ → Prop\n166 |   /-- Plaquettes are ordered 4-tuples of sites forming a square. -/\n167 |   plaquettes : (Λ × Λ × Λ × Λ) → Prop\n168 | \n169 | /-- A gauge field configuration on the lattice: each directed link (x → x + a e_μ)\n170 | carries a group element U(x, μ) ∈ G. -/\n171 | @[ext]\n172 | structure LinkVariable (G : Type) (Λ : Type) : Type 1 where\n173 |   /-- Assigns a group element to each lattice site and direction. -/\n174 |   value : Λ → Fin 4 → G\n175 | \n176 | /--\n177 | The reflection map θ on link variables for any lattice type with `ReflectSite`.\n178 | For a link variable U(n, μ) from site n in direction μ, the reflected\n179 | link variable is:\n180 | \n181 |     (θ U)(n, μ) = U(θ n, μ)⁻¹   if μ = 0 (time direction)\n182 |     (θ U)(n, μ) = U(θ n, μ)     if μ ≠ 0 (spatial direction)\n183 | \n184 | The inverse appears for time-like links because reflection reverses the\n185 | orientation of the link in time.\n186 | -/\n187 | def reflectLinkVariable (N : ℕ) {Λ : Type} [ReflectSite Λ] (U : LinkVariable (SU N) Λ) :\n188 |     LinkVariable (SU N) Λ :=\n189 |   {\n190 |     value := λ n μ =>\n191 |       if μ = 0 then\n192 |         (U.value (ReflectSite.reflectSite n) μ)⁻¹\n193 |       else\n194 |         U.value (ReflectSite.reflectSite n) μ\n195 |   }\n196 | \n197 | /--\n198 | The full geometric reflection is involutive: θ(θ U) = U.\n199 | -/\n200 | lemma reflection_involution (N : ℕ) {Λ : Type} [ReflectSite Λ] (U : LinkVariable (SU N) Λ) :\n201 |     reflectLinkVariable N (reflectLinkVariable N U) = U := by\n202 |   ext n μ\n203 |   dsimp [reflectLinkVariable]\n204 |   have h_inv : ReflectSite.reflectSite (ReflectSite.reflectSite n) = n := ReflectSite.involution n\n205 |   by_cases h : μ = 0\n206 |   · subst h; simp [h_inv]\n207 |   · simp [h, h_inv]\n208 | \n209 | /--\n210 | Convenience alias for `reflectLinkVariable` on `Z4Site` for backward compatibility.\n211 | -/\n212 | def reflectLinkVariableZ4 (N : ℕ) (U : LinkVariable (SU N) Z4Site) : LinkVariable (SU N) Z4Site :=\n213 |   reflectLinkVariable N U\n214 | \n215 | /--\n216 | The full geometric reflection is involutive on Z4Site: θ(θ U) = U.\n217 | -/\n218 | lemma reflection_involution_z4 (N : ℕ) (U : LinkVariable (SU N) Z4Site) :\n219 |     reflectLinkVariableZ4 N (reflectLinkVariableZ4 N U) = U :=\n220 |   reflection_involution N U\n221 | \n222 | section PlaquetteProduct\n223 | \n224 | /--\n225 | The ordered product of link variables around an elementary plaquette in a\n226 | lattice with `AddVector`. For a site n and directions μ, ν, the product traverses:\n227 | \n228 |     n + e_μ + e_ν ←── n + e_ν\n229 |          |              ↑\n\n... 122 more line(s) below (use offset=230 to continue reading)","timestamp":1784083695,"token_count":1272,"tool_call_id":"call_00_yrXQkbA6RFM1fbogxvmp0474","full_token_estimate":947,"tool_meta":{"tool_name":"read_file","file_path":"src/lean/YangMills/Lattice.lean","old_text":null,"new_text":null,"exit_code":null,"line_count":351,"byte_count":12085,"is_error":false,"duration_ms":0,"edit_line":null},"turn":7,"is_prune_marker":false}
