e-time links, and the inner product is in L²(μ₀_on_interface).\n\nWait, but the precise statement in OS Seiler is that:\n\nFor any function A of the gauge fields in the positive-time region:\n\n∫ A(U⁺)·A(θU⁻)·exp(-S_W) = ∫ A*(u)·(TA)(u) dμ⁺⁰(u)\n\nwhere the RHS integrates over the configuration space at time 0 (interface).\n\nLet me check the OS paper for the exact formula. But I don't have direct access to it.\n\nLet me look at the literature references in the code.\n\nActually, I think there's a simpler approach. Let me re-think about what the transfer matrix identity is actually supposed to say.\n\nLet me write out what I think the correct identity should be, using the measure factorization:\n\nUsing the measure factorization μ₀ ≅ μ⁺ × μ⁻ × μ⁰, and the decomposition of S_W:\n\n∫ f(U)·g(θU)·exp(-β·S_W(U)) dμ₀(U)\n\n= ∫_{μ⁺}∫_{μ⁻}∫_{μ⁰} f(U⁺, U⁻, U⁰)·g(θU⁺, θU⁻, θU⁰)·exp(-β·(S_OS⁺(U⁺)+S_OS⁻(U⁻)+S_OS_int(U⁺,U⁻,U⁰))) dμ⁰ dμ⁻ dμ⁺\n\nNow, if we set g = f (as in the reflection positivity case), and we observe that:\n- θU⁺ is on negative sites\n- θU⁻ is on positive sites\n- θU⁰ is on interface sites\n\nLet me denote the reflected configs:\n- U'⁺ = θU⁻ on positive sites\n- U'⁻ = θU⁺ on negative sites\n- U'⁰ = θU⁰ on interface sites\n\nSo f(θU) = f(U'⁺, U'⁻, U'⁰) where U'⁺ = θU⁻, U'⁻ = θU⁺, U'⁰ = θU⁰.\n\nThis is getting confusing. Let me try a different approach.\n\nActually, the key observation is that in the product:\nG(U)·G(θU)\n\nthe factors of G involve f evaluated at U and at θU. But G_plus only evaluates f at configurations where negative links are set to 1.\n\nSo if we want the identity to hold, we need to incorporate the U⁻ dependence into the transfer matrix integral, not into G_plus.\n\nLet me re-examine the definition of G_plus:\n```lean4\nnoncomputable def G_plus (N T L : ℕ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L] (hT : Odd T) (β : ℝ)\n    (f : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L) → ℝ) (cfg : PosInterfaceConfig N T L) : ℝ :=\n  G N T L hT β f (extendLinkVariable N (PeriodicSite T L) (positiveSites T L ∪ interfaceSites T L) cfg)\n```\n\nSo G_plus(cfg) = G(f, extend(cfg)) where extend(cfg) sets negative links to 1.\n\nAnd `G(f, U) = f(U)·exp(-β·S_OS⁺(U))·exp(-β·S_OS_int(U)/2)`.\n\nSo G_plus(cfg) = f(extend(cfg)) · exp(-β·S_OS⁺(extend(cfg))) · exp(-β·S_OS_int(extend(cfg))/2).\n\nNow, S_OS⁺(extend(cfg)) = S_OS⁺(cfg) because S_OS⁺ only depends on positive links, and extend(cfg) has negative links set to 1 but positive links are the same.\n\nS_OS_int(extend(cfg)): this depends on interface links AND possibly on positive/negative links that cross the interface. With negative links set to 1, this gives a different value than with actual negative links.\n\nSo G_plus is NOT the same as G restricted to positive+interface links. It's G with negative links artificially set to 1.\n\nThis means the identity as stated cannot hold in general. Let me reconsider.\n\nHmm wait, maybe I'm overcomplicating this. Let me look at the definition of the transfer matrix more carefully.\n\nThe transfer matrix includes S_OS_int of the FULL configuration (including negative links). So:\n\n(T G_plus)(u) = ∫ G_plus(restrict(merge(U⁻, u)))·exp(-β·S_OS_int(extendToFull(U⁻, u))) dμ⁻(U⁻)\n\nBut G_plus(restrict(merge(U⁻, u))) = G_plus(u) by restrict_merge_id.\n\nSo:\n(T G_plus)(u) = G_plus(u)·∫ exp(-β·S_OS_int(extendToFull(U⁻, u))) dμ⁻(U⁻)\n\nAnd the RHS of the identity is:\n∫ G_plus(u)·(T G_plus)(u) dμ⁺⁰(u) = ∫ (G_plus(u))²·(∫ exp(-β·S_OS_int(full(U⁻, u))) dμ⁻(U⁻)) dμ⁺⁰(u)\n\nNow, the LHS is:\n∫ G(U)·G(θU) dμ₀(U)\n\nUsing measure factorization:\n= ∫_{μ⁺}∫_{μ⁻}∫_{μ⁰} G(U⁺, U⁻, U⁰)·G(θU⁺, θU⁻, θU⁰) dμ⁰ dμ⁻ dμ⁺\n\nLet me expand G:\nG(U⁺, U⁻, U⁰) = f(U⁺, U⁻, U⁰)·exp(-β·S_OS⁺(U⁺))·exp(-β·S_OS_int(U⁺, U⁻, U⁰)/2)\n\nG(θU⁺, θU⁻, θU⁰) = f(θU⁺, θU⁻, θU⁰)·exp(-β·S_OS⁺(θU⁺))·exp(-β·S_OS_int(θU⁺, θU⁻, θU⁰)/2)\n\nNow, S_OS⁺(θU⁺) = S_OS⁻(U⁻) (reflection swaps positive and negative)\nS_OS_int(θU⁺, θU⁻, θU⁰) = S_OS_int(U⁺, U⁻, U⁰) (interface is invariant under reflection)\n\nSo:\nG(θU) = f(