tandard OS formalism, the Gibbs measure is:\ndν(U) = (1/Z)·exp(-β·S_W(U)) dμ₀(U)\n\nAnd the reflection positivity condition is:\n∫ F*(U)·F(θU) dν(U) ≥ 0\n\nfor any F that depends on the positive-time links only.\n\nIn our case, we have:\n∫ f(U)·f(θU) dν(U)\n\nand we want to show this is ≥ 0. But f is not necessarily supported on positive links!\n\nHowever, we can write:\nf(U)·f(θU)·exp(-β·S_W(U)) = G(U)·G(θU)\n\nwhere G(U) = f(U)·exp(-β·S_OS⁺(U))·exp(-β·S_OS_int(U)/2)\n\nNow, the function G(U) may still depend on all links through f. But in the OS construction, the transfer matrix acts on G restricted to positive+interface links.\n\nActually, I think the correct approach is different. Let me re-read the OS paper definition of the transfer matrix.\n\nIn Osterwalder-Seiler, the transfer matrix is defined as:\n(Tψ)(U⁺, U⁰) = ∫ ψ(U⁻, U⁰)·exp(-S_int(U⁺, U⁻, U⁰)) dμ⁻(U⁻)\n\nAnd the G functions in the identity are such that:\nG(U⁺, U⁻, U⁰) = ψ(U⁺, U⁰)·exp(-S_OS⁺(U⁺)/2)\n\nfor some ψ that depends only on (U⁺, U⁰).\n\nWait, but in our code:\nG(U) = f(U)·exp(-β·S_OS⁺(U))·exp(-β·S_OS_int(U)/2)\n\nThis is NOT factorized as ψ(U⁺, U⁰)·exp(-S_OS⁺(U⁺)/2) because f can depend on negative links.\n\nSo the issue is fundamental: the definition of G mixes positive and negative link dependence.\n\nHmm wait, let me look at the factorization again:\n\nIn `gibbsExpectationPeriodic_reflection_positive`, the factorization is:\n\nReal.exp(-β * S_total cfg) = \n  (Real.exp(-β * S_OS_positive) * Real.exp(-β * S_OS_interface / 2)) *\n  (Real.exp(-β * S_OS_positive_reflected) * Real.exp(-β * S_OS_interface_reflected / 2))\n\nAnd this is used to define:\n\nG(U) = f(U) * exp(-β * S_OS_positive(U)) * exp(-β * S_OS_interface(U) / 2)\n\nG(θU) = f(θU) * exp(-β * S_OS_positive(θU)) * exp(-β * S_OS_interface(θU) / 2)\n\nAnd indeed G(U)·G(θU) = f(U)·f(θU)·exp(-β·S_W(U)).\n\nNow, the transfer matrix approach is supposed to show that the integral of G(U)·G(θU) is non-negative.\n\nBut G involves f(U) which can depend on negative links. So G_plus (with negative links set to 1) is NOT what appears in the LHS of the desired identity.\n\nI think the resolution is that the transfer matrix identity needs to be applied to G_plus which is defined as:\n\nG_plus(U⁺, U⁰) = G(U⁺, 𝟙, U⁰)\n\nAnd then the identity is:\n\n∫ G(U)·G(θU) dμ₀ = ∫ G_plus(u)·(T' G_plus)(u) dμ⁺⁰(u)\n\nwhere T' is a DIFFERENT transfer matrix that includes the effect of integrating out the negative links with f rather than setting them to 1.\n\nHmm, but this would mean the current definition of T is wrong too.\n\nActually, I think the problem is that the transfer matrix is supposed to act on functions of the interface configuration (time-0 links), not on functions of the positive+interface config. Let me re-read the OS paper.\n\nActually, let me search the literature for the exact statement.","turn":8,"is_prune_marker":false}
