{"id":56,"role":"Tool","content":"Search results (5):\n\n1. [https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/1978AnPhy.110..440O/abstract]\n   Gauge field theories on a lattice - NASA/ADS\n   This implies the existence of a positive self-adjoint transfer matrix. We then prove existence and analyticity of the infinite volume limit of strongly coupled Yang-Mills theories on the lattice and we verify Wilson's confinement bound. Finally we present a rigorous treatment of the Higgs mechanism in lattice gauge theories.\n\n2. [https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/0003491678900398]\n   Gauge field theories on a lattice - ScienceDirect\n   We begin a rigorous, nonperturbative investigation of quantum field theories with local internal symmetries. We discuss the lattice approximation of Yang-Mills fields and of fermion fields in the Euclidean setup and we verify physical positivity for the Schwinger functions of these approximations. This implies the existence of a positive self-adjoint transfer matrix. We then prove existence ...\n\n3. [https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/0003491678900398]\n   Gauge field theories on a lattice - ScienceDirect\n   This implies the existence of a positive self-adjoint transfer matrix. We then prove existence and analyticity of the infinite volume limit of strongly coupled Yang-Mills theories on the lattice and we verify Wilson's confinement bound. Finally we present a rigorous treatment of the Higgs mechanism in lattice gauge theories.\n\n4. [https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Gauge-field-theories-on-a-lattice-Osterwalder-Seiler/610728f713f24d54488c5e5be85d5d96092211e3]\n   Gauge field theories on a lattice - Semantic Scholar\n   This implies the existence of a positive self-adjoint transfer matrix. We then prove existence and analyticity of the infinite volume limit of strongly coupled Yang-Mills theories on the lattice and we verify Wilson's confinement bound. Finally we present a rigorous treatment of the Higgs mechanism in lattice gauge theories.\n\n5. [https://www.bibsonomy.org/bibtex/12499deda4efb08cf6df8a06f0b844464]\n   Gauge field theories on a lattice - BibSonomy\n   This implies the existence of a positive self-adjoint transfer matrix. We then prove existence and analyticity of the infinite volume limit of strongly coupled Yang-Mills theories on the lattice and we verify Wilson's confinement bound. Finally we present a rigorous treatment of the Higgs mechanism in lattice gauge theories.\n\n","timestamp":1784084133,"token_count":611,"tool_call_id":"call_00_RzjHo6sKvEUmwcYCCrOr1061","full_token_estimate":566,"tool_meta":{"tool_name":"web_search","file_path":null,"old_text":"Osterwalder Seiler \"gauge field theories on a lattice\" transfer matrix formula explicit","new_text":null,"exit_code":null,"line_count":null,"byte_count":2431,"is_error":false,"duration_ms":995,"edit_line":null},"turn":20,"is_prune_marker":false}
