{"id":93,"role":"Tool","content":"C:\\github\\YangMills\\src\\lean\\YangMills\\Proofs\\ReflectionPositivity.lean\n-- 1526 lines, 94678 bytes --\n 50 | /--\n 51 | The expectation-like pairing for reflection positivity on ℤ⁴.\n 52 | \n 53 | Given a Wilson action S_W and a reference measure dU (product Haar measure),\n 54 | the expectation of an observable F is:\n 55 | \n 56 |     ⟨F⟩ = (1/Z) ∫ F(U) exp(-S_W[U]) dU\n 57 | \n 58 | For the factorization lemma, we only need the formal algebraic structure\n 59 | of this expression. The actual integration theory (Haar measure, product\n 60 | measure, partition function) is available in Mathlib but requires heavy\n 61 | infrastructure. Here we give the symbolic manipulation that underlies\n 62 | the reflection positivity proof.\n 63 | \n 64 | ⚠️ **Known limitation**: The `linearity` field requires integrability hypotheses\n 65 | on `F(extend...)*exp(-β*S)` and `G(extend...)*exp(-β*S)`. This is mathematically\n 66 | correct (linearity of expectation requires integrability). The `reflectionPositive`\n 67 | field relies on `gibbsExpectationZ4_reflection_positive` which has the `hadd` issue\n 68 | documented in `docs/hadd_issue.md`.\n 69 | -/\n 70 | structure Z4Expectation (N : ℕ) (β : ℝ) (sites : Finset Z4Site) : Type 1 where\n 71 |   /-- The partition function Z = ∫ exp(-S_W) dU. -/\n 72 |   partitionFunction : ℝ\n 73 |   /-- Positivity of the partition function: Z > 0 for β > 0. -/\n 74 |   partitionFunctionPos : partitionFunction > 0\n 75 |   /--\n 76 |   The expectation of an observable F, symbolically:\n 77 |       ⟨F⟩ = (1/Z) ∫ F(U) exp(-S_W[U]) dU\n 78 |   -/\n 79 |   evaluate : (LinkVariable (SU N) Z4Site → ℝ) → ℝ\n 80 |   /--\n 81 |   The expectation is linear: ⟨aF + bG⟩ = a⟨F⟩ + b⟨G⟩,\n 82 |   provided the integrands F(U) exp(-β S_W[U]) and G(U) exp(-β S_W[U]) are integrable\n 83 |   with respect to the product Haar measure.\n 84 |   -/\n 85 |   linearity : ∀ (a b : ℝ) (F G : LinkVariable (SU N) Z4Site → ℝ),\n 86 |     (MeasureTheory.Integrable (λ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfigZ4 N sites) => F (extendLinkVariableZ4 N sites cfg) *\n 87 |       Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionFiniteConfigZ4 N β sites cfg)) (productHaarMeasureZ4 N sites)) →\n 88 |     (MeasureTheory.Integrable (λ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfigZ4 N sites) => G (extendLinkVariableZ4 N sites cfg) *\n 89 |       Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionFiniteConfigZ4 N β sites cfg)) (productHaarMeasureZ4 N sites)) →\n 90 |     evaluate (λ U => a * F U + b * G U) = a * evaluate F + b * evaluate G\n 91 |   /--\n 92 |   The expectation is normalized: ⟨1⟩ = 1.\n 93 |   -/\n 94 |   normalization : evaluate (λ _ => 1) = 1\n 95 |   /--\n 96 |   The expectation is positive: if F ≥ 0 pointwise, then ⟨F⟩ ≥ 0.\n 97 |   -/\n 98 |   positivity : ∀ (F : LinkVariable (SU N) Z4Site → ℝ),\n 99 |     (∀ U, F U ≥ 0) → evaluate F ≥ 0\n100 |   /--\n101 |   Reflection positivity: for any observable f, we have ⟨f θ(f)⟩ ≥ 0.\n102 |   \n103 |   This is the conclusion of the Osterwalder-Seiler factorization lemma:\n104 |   the expectation of f θ(f) is an L² norm squared, hence non-negative.\n105 |   -/\n106 |   reflectionPositive : ∀ (f : LinkVariable (SU N) Z4Site → ℝ),\n107 |     evaluate (λ U => f U * reflectObservableZ4 N f U) ≥ 0\n108 | \n109 | /--\n110 | Construct a `Z4Expectation` for the Wilson action on a finite ℤ⁴ lattice.\n111 | This provides the reflection positivity certificate for the Wilson action.\n112 | -/\n113 | noncomputable def wilsonZ4Expectation (N : ℕ) (β : ℝ) (sites : Finset Z4Site)\n114 |     (hadd : ∀ n, n ∈ sites → addVector n 0 ∈ sites)\n115 |     (hsites : ∀ n, n ∈ sites → reflectSite n ∈ sites) : Z4Expectation N β sites :=\n116 |   {\n117 |     partitionFunction := partitionFunctionFiniteZ4 N β sites\n118 |     partitionFunctionPos := partitionFunctionFiniteZ4_pos N β sites\n119 |     evaluate := gibbsExpectationZ4 N β sites\n120 |     linearity := λ a b F G hF hG => gibbsExpectationZ4_linear N β sites a b F G hF hG\n121 |     normalization := gibbsExpectationZ4_normalization N β sites\n122 |     positivity := λ F hF => gibbsExpectationZ4_pos N β sites F hF\n123 |     reflectionPositive := λ f => \n124 |       gibbsExpectationZ4_reflection_positive N β sites hadd hsites f\n125 |   }\n126 | \n127 | /--\n128 | The SU(N) lattice Yang-Mills measure with the Wilson action on any finite ℤ⁴ lattice\n129 | satisfying the closure conditions `hadd` and `hsites` is reflection positive.\n130 | \n131 | ⚠️ **Status**: Validated by the Lean kernel. The proof of `gibbsExpectationZ4_reflection_positive`\n132 | is mathematically vacuous for nonempty finite lattices due to the `hadd` issue (see\n133 | `docs/hadd_issue.md`). A complete proof requires implementing periodic boundary conditions\n134 | and the Osterwalder-Seiler factorization.\n135 | -/\n136 | theorem lattice_ym_reflection_positive (N : ℕ) (β : ℝ) (hβ : β > 0)\n137 |     (sites : Finset Z4Site) (hadd : ∀ n, n ∈ sites → addVector n 0 ∈ sites)\n138 |     (hsites : ∀ n, n ∈ sites → reflectSite n ∈ sites) :\n139 |     ∀ (f : LinkVariable (SU N) Z4Site → ℝ),\n140 |       (wilsonZ4Expectation N β sites hadd hsites).evaluate (λ U => f U * reflectObservableZ4 N f U) ≥ 0 := by\n141 |   intro f\n142 |   exact (wilsonZ4Expectation N β sites hadd hsites).reflectionPositive f\n143 | \n144 | /-! ### Periodic Lattice (PeriodicSite) -/\n145 | \n146 | section PeriodicSite\n147 | \n148 | open scoped BigOperators\n149 | \n\n... 1377 more line(s) below (use offset=150 to continue reading)","timestamp":1784084313,"token_count":1675,"tool_call_id":"call_00_gwePpW5FXpamjbayF92s8924","full_token_estimate":1234,"tool_meta":{"tool_name":"read_file","file_path":"src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/ReflectionPositivity.lean","old_text":null,"new_text":null,"exit_code":null,"line_count":1526,"byte_count":94678,"is_error":false,"duration_ms":0,"edit_line":null},"turn":37,"is_prune_marker":false}
{"id":94,"role":"Assistant","content":"Now I have a clear picture. The lemma `gibbsExpectationPeriodic_reflection_positive` as stated is mathematically false — it claims reflection positivity for ALL functions f, but the standard OS theorem only guarantees it for functions supported on positive+interface links. The `transferMatrix_identity` is also incorrect because `G_plus` sets negative links to 1 while the full `G` uses actual negative links.\n\nLet me implement the fixes.","timestamp":1784084318,"token_count":113,"tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"path\": \"src/lean/YangMills/Overview.lean\"}","name":"read_file"},"id":"call_00_jWscOjYzTFq01lp0ieGx4462","type":"function"}],"full_token_estimate":349,"reasoning_content":"Now I can see the full picture. Both the Z4Site and PeriodicSite versions of the structure claim reflection positivity for ALL f, which is mathematically incorrect.\n\nThe fix should be applied to both structures, but since the Z4Site version has the hadd issue (making it vacuous for nonempty lattices), I'll focus on the PeriodicSite version.\n\nLet me now make the minimal changes:\n\n1. Define `supportedOnPosInterface` in `ReflectionPositivity.lean`\n2. Update `gibbsExpectationPeriodic_reflection_positive` to require this hypothesis\n3. Update `PeriodicExpectation` to require it in the `reflectionPositive` field\n4. Update `wilsonPeriodicExpectation` and `lattice_ym_reflection_positive_periodic`\n5. Update `TransferMatrix.lean` to note the issue\n\nLet me also update `integral_G_thetaG_nonneg` to note its dependency on the incorrect identity.\n\nLet me start with the changes.","turn":38,"is_prune_marker":false}
{"id":95,"role":"Tool","content":"C:\\github\\YangMills\\src\\lean\\YangMills\\Overview.lean\n-- 107 lines, 6111 bytes --\n  1 | /-\n  2 | # Overview\n  3 | \n  4 | Project structure, references, and current status for the Yang-Mills\n  5 | formalization effort.\n  6 | \n  7 | ## Current Status (Phase 6: Periodic boundary conditions — genuine reflection positivity proof)\n  8 | \n  9 | ### Completed (Phase 3):\n 10 | - SU(N) defined via Mathlib's `Matrix.specialUnitaryGroup` (SpecialUnitary.lean)\n 11 | - su(N) Lie algebra as skew-Hermitian traceless matrices (SpecialUnitary.lean)\n 12 | - CompactSpace (SU N) proved (SpecialUnitary.lean)\n 13 | - Principal G-bundles, connections, curvature (GaugeTheory.lean)\n 14 | - Yang-Mills action functional (GaugeTheory.lean)\n 15 | - Lattice gauge theory foundations (Lattice.lean)\n 16 | - OS Axioms skeleton (OSAxioms.lean)\n 17 | - Mass Gap definition (MassGap.lean)\n 18 | \n 19 | ### Completed (Phase 4 — Z4Site combinatorial lemmas):\n 20 | - **reflectSite_involution**: reflectSite ∘ reflectSite = id\n 21 | - **plaquette_product_reflection_spatial**: plaquette product reflection for spatial μ,ν\n 22 | - **trace_plaquette_product_reflection**: trace equality for ALL (μ,ν) cases including time-involving\n 23 | - **neg_action_reflection_z4**: S_W⁻[U] = S_W⁺[θU] (with hadd hypothesis)\n 24 | - **interface_action_reflection_symmetric_z4**: S_W⁰[θU] = S_W⁰[U] (with hadd hypothesis)\n 25 | - **reflectTriple_preserves_interface**: reflection maps interface plaquettes to interface plaquettes\n 26 | - **total_wilson_action_decomposition_z4**: S_W = S_W⁺ + S_W⁻ + S_W⁰\n 27 | - **wilsonActionFiniteConfig_reflection_invariant**: S_W[θU] = S_W[U]\n 28 | - **extend_reflectFiniteConfig_eq**: extending reflected config = reflecting extended config\n 29 | \n 30 | ### Completed (Phase 5 — Measure-theoretic formalization):\n 31 | - **productHaarMeasure**: product Haar measure on finite lattice via Measure.pi\n 32 | - **MeasurableSpace on LinkVariable**: via MeasurableSpace.comap on value projection\n 33 | - **IsProbabilityMeasure**: total volume = 1 (proved)\n 34 | - **partitionFunctionFinite_pos**: > 0 for any sites (including nonempty)\n 35 | - **gibbsExpectation_pos**: expectation of non-negative observable is ≥ 0\n 36 | - **gibbsExpectation_normalization**: ⟨1⟩ = 1\n 37 | - **gibbsExpectation_linear**: linearity of expectation with integrability hypotheses\n 38 | - **gibbsExpectationZ4_reflection_positive**: proved (vacuous for nonempty due to hadd)\n 39 | - **measurable_extendLinkVariable**: extension map is measurable\n 40 | - **measurable_wilsonActionFiniteConfig**: Wilson action is measurable (continuous on compact)\n 41 | \n 42 | ### Completed (Phase 6 — Periodic BCs, Osterwalder-Seiler decomposition):\n 43 | - **PeriodicSite**: finite lattice with ZMod time and spatial coordinates\n 44 | - **addVectorPeriodic, reflectSitePeriodic**: modular arithmetic for periodic BCs\n 45 | - **signedTime**: signed lift of ZMod T to ℤ, enabling time-ordered decomposition\n 46 | - **positiveSites, negativeSites, interfaceSites**: time-slice partitioning\n 47 | - **wilsonActionOSPositive/Negative/Interface**: OS plaquette-based decomposition\n 48 | - **plaquette_classification**: every plaquette is positive, negative, or interface\n 49 | - **total_decomposition_os_periodic**: S_W = S_OS⁺ + S_OS⁻ + S_OS_int\n 50 | - **reflectPlaquetteIndex_sign**: reflection flips positive ↔ negative plaquettes\n 51 | - **plaquettePositive/Negative**: predicates for OS classification\n 52 | - **reflectPlaquetteIndex**: involutive bijection on PlaquetteIndex\n 53 | - **trace_plaquetteProduct_reflect_all**: unconditional trace equality for all (μ,ν)\n 54 | - **plaquetteContribution_reflect_eq_all**: unconditional contribution equality\n 55 | - **neg_action_reflection_os_periodic**: S_OS⁻[U] = S_OS⁺[θU] via Fintype.sum_equiv\n 56 | - **interface_action_reflection_symmetric_os_periodic**: S_OS_int[θU] = S_OS_int[U]\n 57 | - **gibbsExpectationPeriodic_reflection_positive**: all algebraic steps complete,\n 58 |   reduction to ∫ G·θG dμ₀ ≥ 0 proved. Final positivity depends on the\n 59 |   Peter–Weyl theorem on SU(N) (transfer matrix argument) — one `sorry` remains.\n 60 | \n 61 | ### Remaining (1 sorry item):\n 62 | - **gibbsExpectationPeriodic_reflection_positive**: ∫ G·θG dμ₀ ≥ 0 requires the\n 63 |   transfer matrix positivity argument (Osterwalder-Seiler 1979, §3). This needs\n 64 |   the Peter–Weyl theorem on SU(N) or spectral theory of compact operators on\n 65 |   L²(SU(N)). See the comment in ReflectionPositivity.lean for full details.\n 66 |   A proof sketch and gap analysis are in `Proofs/TransferMatrix.lean` and\n 67 |   `docs/gap_analysis.md`.\n 68 | \n 69 | ### In Progress:\n 70 | - **PositiveDefinite.lean**: Framework for positive-definite functions on groups.\n 71 |   Defines the predicate, proves characters are positive-definite, and states the\n 72 |   key fact (exp(c Re Tr(g)) positive-definite) as a lemma depending on Peter-Weyl.\n 73 | - **TransferMatrix.lean**: Proof sketch with transfer matrix definition,\n 74 |   measure factorization, and key identity. `mergeConfigurations` now implemented.\n 75 |   The remaining `sorry` items are: measure factorization, key identity,\n 76 |   and transfer matrix positivity (the latter requires Peter-Weyl).\n 77 | \n 78 | ### Future work:\n 79 | - Complete the transfer matrix positivity proof (Peter–Weyl theorem)\n 80 | - Construct the `PeriodicExpectation` structure (defined but uses `sorry`)\n 81 | - Continuum limit (Balaban renormalization group)\n 82 | - OS reconstruction theorem (Euclidean → Minkowski reconstruction)\n 83 | - Mass gap proof (positivity and exponential decay)\n 84 | - Construct the `PeriodicExpectation` structure (defined but uses `sorry`)\n 85 | - Continuum limit (Balaban renormalization group)\n 86 | - OS reconstruction theorem (Euclidean → Minkowski reconstruction)\n 87 | - Mass gap proof (positivity and exponential decay)\n 88 | \n 89 | ## References\n 90 | \n 91 | - A. Jaffe, E. Witten, \"Quantum Yang-Mills Theory\" (Clay Millennium Problem)\n 92 | - R. Streater, A. Wightman, \"PCT, Spin and Statistics, and All That\"\n 93 | - J. Glimm, A. Jaffe, \"Quantum Physics: A Functional Integral Point of View\"\n 94 | - K. Osterwalder, R. Schrader, \"Axioms for Euclidean Green's Functions\"\n 95 | - K. Osterwalder, E. Seiler, \"Gauge Field Theories on a Lattice\" (1979)\n 96 | - T. Balaban, \"Renormalization group approach to lattice gauge field theories\"\n 97 | - M. Hairer, \"A theory of regularity structures\"\n 98 | - S. Chatterjee, \"Yang-Mills for probabilists\"\n 99 | - K. Wilson, \"Confinement of quarks\"\n100 | -/\n101 | \n102 | namespace YangMills\n103 | \n104 | def description : String :=\n105 |   \"Formalization of Yang-Mills existence and mass gap problem (Clay Millennium Prize)\"\n106 | \n107 | end YangMills\n","timestamp":1784084318,"token_count":2113,"tool_call_id":"call_00_jWscOjYzTFq01lp0ieGx4462","full_token_estimate":1551,"tool_meta":{"tool_name":"read_file","file_path":"src/lean/YangMills/Overview.lean","old_text":null,"new_text":null,"exit_code":null,"line_count":107,"byte_count":6111,"is_error":false,"duration_ms":0,"edit_line":null},"turn":38,"is_prune_marker":false}
