{"id":135,"role":"Tool","content":"C:\\github\\YangMills\\src\\lean\\YangMills\\Proofs\\ReflectionPositivity.lean\n-- 1549 lines, 96263 bytes --\n286 |       rfl\n287 | \n288 | /--\n289 | A function `f : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L) → ℝ` depends only on\n290 | positive-time and interface (time-0) links iff its value is determined by\n291 | the values of the link variable on `positiveSites T L ∪ interfaceSites T L`.\n292 | This is the correct hypothesis for the Osterwalder-Seiler reflection positivity\n293 | theorem: only observables localized in the positive-time region (including the\n294 | interface at time 0) are required to satisfy ⟨θf, f⟩ ≥ 0.\n295 | \n296 | ⚠️ **Mathematical note**: The lemma `gibbsExpectationPeriodic_reflection_positive`\n297 | as originally stated (without this hypothesis) is **false** in general.  A\n298 | counterexample exists even for β=0 (free theory): take\n299 | `f(U) = a(U(ℓ))·b(U(θℓ)) - a(U(θℓ))·b(U(ℓ))` for a positive-site link ℓ\n300 | and its reflection θℓ.  Then `f·θf = -(f)²` and its integral is strictly negative.\n301 | The hypothesis that `f` depends only on positive+interface links excludes such\n302 | counterexamples.\n303 | -/\n304 | def dependsOnlyOnPosInterface (N T L : ℕ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L]\n305 |     (f : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L) → ℝ) : Prop :=\n\n... 1244 more line(s) below (use offset=306 to continue reading)","timestamp":1784084462,"token_count":423,"tool_call_id":"call_00_ok5vCNKpdMrjLGvETkay5458","full_token_estimate":325,"tool_meta":{"tool_name":"read_file","file_path":"src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/ReflectionPositivity.lean","old_text":null,"new_text":null,"exit_code":null,"line_count":1549,"byte_count":96263,"is_error":false,"duration_ms":0,"edit_line":null},"turn":58,"is_prune_marker":false}
