{"id":152,"role":"Tool","content":"C:\\github\\YangMills\\src\\lean\\YangMills\\Proofs\\ReflectionPositivity.lean\n-- 1549 lines, 96144 bytes --\n1460 |       -- A previous attempt at this proof (`transferMatrix_identity` in\n1461 |       -- `TransferMatrix.lean`) is **mathematically incorrect**.  It defined\n1462 |       -- G_plus(U⁺,U⁰) = G(U⁺,𝟙,U⁰) (setting negative links to 1) and claimed\n1463 |       --   ∫ G(U)·G(θU) dμ₀ = ∫ G_plus·(T G_plus) dμ⁺⁰\n1464 |       -- This identity is false for general f because G_plus evaluates S_OS_int\n1465 |       -- at (U⁺,𝟙,U⁰) while the full G evaluates it at (U⁺,U⁻,U⁰), and the\n1466 |       -- `transferMatrix_positive` lemma reduces T to a multiplication operator\n1467 |       -- (via `restrict_merge_id`), which trivializes the transfer matrix.\n1468 |       --\n1469 |       -- The correct approach requires redefining the transfer matrix T to act on\n1470 |       -- functions of the POSITIVE+INTERFACE configuration (as above), with T\n1471 |       -- integrating over negative links AND applying the reflection θ⁻⁰ to the\n1472 |       -- argument.  This is mathematically nontrivial and is left as future work.\n1473 |       --\n1474 |       -- Once the correct identity is formalized, replace this `sorry` with:\n1475 |       --   rw [correct_identity N T L hT β f hf_supported]\n1476 |       --   apply transferMatrix_positive' N T L β f hf_supported\n1477 |       --\n1478 |       -- where `transferMatrix_positive'` proves positivity of the correctly defined T.\n1479 |       --\n1480 |       -- REFERENCES:\n1481 |       --   - K. Osterwalder, E. Seiler, \"Gauge Field Theories on a Lattice\"\n1482 |       --     (Ann. Phys. 110, 1978, pp 440–471), §3.\n1483 |       --   - J. Glimm, A. Jaffe, \"Quantum Physics\" (2nd ed.), §6.1.\n1484 |       --   - M. Lüscher, \"Some analytic results concerning the mass spectrum\n1485 |       --     of Yang-Mills gauge theories on a torus\" (1983)\n1486 |       --   - M. Salmhofer, \"Construction of a Higgs field\" (thesis, 1990).\n1487 |       sorry\n1488 | end OSDecomposition\n1489 | /--\n1490 | The `PeriodicExpectation` structure for the SU(N) Wilson action on a finite periodic lattice.\n1491 | This provides a reflection positivity certificate that does NOT require the `hadd` hypothesis,\n1492 | because periodic boundary conditions make the lattice closed under forward time translation.\n1493 | -/\n1494 | structure PeriodicExpectation (N T L : ℕ) (β : ℝ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L] (hT : Odd T) : Type 1 where\n1495 |   /-- The partition function Z = ∫ exp(-S_W) dU. -/\n1496 |   partitionFunction : ℝ\n1497 |   /-- Positivity of the partition function: Z > 0 for β > 0. -/\n1498 |   partitionFunctionPos : partitionFunction > 0\n1499 |   /-- The expectation of an observable F. -/\n1500 |   evaluate : (LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L) → ℝ) → ℝ\n1501 |   /-- Linearity of expectation. -/\n1502 |   linearity : ∀ (a b : ℝ) (F G : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L) → ℝ),\n1503 |     (MeasureTheory.Integrable (λ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfig N (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L))) =>\n1504 |       F (extendLinkVariable N (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)) cfg) *\n1505 |       Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionFiniteConfig N β (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)) cfg))\n1506 |       (productHaarMeasure N (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)))) →\n1507 |     (MeasureTheory.Integrable (λ (cfg : FiniteLinkConfig N (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L))) =>\n1508 |       G (extendLinkVariable N (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)) cfg) *\n1509 |       Real.exp (-β * wilsonActionFiniteConfig N β (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)) cfg))\n1510 |       (productHaarMeasure N (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)))) →\n1511 |     evaluate (λ U => a * F U + b * G U) = a * evaluate F + b * evaluate G\n1512 |   /-- Normalization: ⟨1⟩ = 1. -/\n1513 |   normalization : evaluate (λ _ => 1) = 1\n1514 |   /-- Reflection positivity: if f depends only on positive+interface links, then ⟨f · θ(f)⟩ ≥ 0. -/\n1515 |   reflectionPositive : ∀ (f : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L) → ℝ),\n1516 |     dependsOnlyOnPosInterface N T L f →\n1517 |     evaluate (λ U => f U * reflectObservable N f U) ≥ 0\n1518 | \n1519 | /--\n1520 | Construct a `PeriodicExpectation` for the Wilson action on a finite periodic lattice.\n1521 | This uses the Osterwalder-Seiler factorization to prove reflection positivity without\n1522 | the `hadd` limitation of the Z4Site version.\n1523 | -/\n1524 | noncomputable def wilsonPeriodicExpectation (N T L : ℕ) (β : ℝ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L] (hT : Odd T) :\n1525 |     PeriodicExpectation N T L β hT :=\n1526 |   {\n1527 |     partitionFunction := partitionFunctionFinite N β (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L))\n1528 |     partitionFunctionPos := partitionFunctionFinite_pos N β (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L))\n1529 |     evaluate := gibbsExpectation N β (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L))\n1530 |     linearity := λ a b F G hF hG =>\n1531 |       gibbsExpectation_linear N β (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)) a b F G hF hG\n1532 |     normalization := gibbsExpectation_normalization N β (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L))\n1533 |     positivity := λ F hF => gibbsExpectation_pos N β (PeriodicSite T L) (Finset.univ : Finset (PeriodicSite T L)) F hF\n1534 |     reflectionPositive := λ f hf_supported =>\n1535 |       gibbsExpectationPeriodic_reflection_positive N T L β hT f hf_supported\n1536 |   }\n1537 | /--\n1538 | The SU(N) lattice Yang-Mills measure with the Wilson action on a finite periodic lattice\n1539 | is reflection positive for observables that depend only on links in the positive-time\n1540 | and interface (time-0) regions.  This is the content of the Osterwalder-Seiler theorem.\n1541 | -/\n1542 | theorem lattice_ym_reflection_positive_periodic (N T L : ℕ) (β : ℝ) [NeZero T] [NeZero L] (hβ : β > 0) (hT : Odd T) :\n1543 |     ∀ (f : LinkVariable (SU N) (PeriodicSite T L) → ℝ),\n1544 |       dependsOnlyOnPosInterface N T L f →\n1545 |       (wilsonPeriodicExpectation N T L β hT).evaluate (λ U => f U * reflectObservable N f U) ≥ 0 := by\n1546 |   intro f hf_supported\n1547 |   exact (wilsonPeriodicExpectation N T L β hT).reflectionPositive f hf_supported\n1548 | \n1549 | end PeriodicSite\n","timestamp":1784084522,"token_count":2014,"tool_call_id":"call_00_m9PsDu9avTYfOJH3cjEo7327","full_token_estimate":1474,"tool_meta":{"tool_name":"read_file","file_path":"src/lean/YangMills/Proofs/ReflectionPositivity.lean","old_text":null,"new_text":null,"exit_code":null,"line_count":1549,"byte_count":96144,"is_error":false,"duration_ms":0,"edit_line":null},"turn":66,"is_prune_marker":false}
